{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.GibbsRatioMonotonicity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.GibbsRatioMonotonicity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Exp","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.GibbsRatioMonotonicity.target_unreachable_of_gt_initial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.GibbsRatioMonotonicity.target_unreachable_of_gt_initial","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GibbsRatioMonotonicity.lean#L195-L205","doc":"**The exclusion.** A growth target strictly above the undamped value `R 0`\nis unreachable by *every* damping time `τ ≥ 0` — canonical or fitted. This is\nthe shape of a one-parameter-family exclusion: it forecloses tuning `τ` as a\nfit escape, rather than merely reporting that one particular `τ` missed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.GibbsRatioMonotonicity.ratio_le_initial_of_energies_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.GibbsRatioMonotonicity.ratio_le_initial_of_energies_le","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GibbsRatioMonotonicity.lean#L187-L193","doc":"**Damping cannot raise the growth ratio** when the energy ranges separate:\n`R τ ≤ R 0` for every `τ ≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.GibbsRatioMonotonicity.target_unreachable_of_coupling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.GibbsRatioMonotonicity.target_unreachable_of_coupling","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GibbsRatioMonotonicity.lean#L172-L185","doc":"**The exclusion, in its applicable form.** Given a dominating coupling, a\ngrowth target strictly above the undamped value `R 0` is unreachable by every\n`τ ≥ 0`. This is the statement that closes the GAP-6 family exclusion modulo the\nfinite CDF check that produces the coupling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.GibbsRatioMonotonicity.ratio_le_initial_of_coupling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.GibbsRatioMonotonicity.ratio_le_initial_of_coupling","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GibbsRatioMonotonicity.lean#L160-L170","doc":"**Damping cannot raise the growth ratio** when a dominating coupling exists.\nThe applicable form of the exclusion for overlapping energy ranges. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.GibbsRatioMonotonicity.crossSum_le_of_coupling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.GibbsRatioMonotonicity.crossSum_le_of_coupling","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GibbsRatioMonotonicity.lean#L108-L158","doc":"**Sufficient condition via a coupling (the usable one).** The termwise test\n`∀ i j, C i ≤ D j` is far too strong — it fails whenever the two energy ranges\noverlap, as they do for the Δ_λ data. The right hypothesis is a **coupling**:\na non-negative matrix `M` with the prescribed row/column marginals, supported\nonly on pairs where `C i ≤ D j`. Then the comparison holds termwise *along the\ncoupling* rather than for all pairs.\n\nBy the standard characterisation, such a coupling exists exactly when the\nnumerator's energy distribution **first-order stochastically dominates** the\ndenominator's — a finite, checkable condition on the two CDFs. For the Δ_λ data\nit **holds** (0 violations across all 43 thresholds), which is what makes this\nthe applicable route where `crossSum_le_of_energies_le` is not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.GibbsRatioMonotonicity.crossSum_le_of_energies_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.GibbsRatioMonotonicity.crossSum_le_of_energies_le","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GibbsRatioMonotonicity.lean#L94-L106","doc":"**Sufficient condition, termwise.** If every denominator energy is at most\nevery numerator energy, then for `τ ≥ 0` the criterion holds termwise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.GibbsRatioMonotonicity.ratio_le_initial_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.GibbsRatioMonotonicity.ratio_le_initial_iff","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GibbsRatioMonotonicity.lean#L73-L92","doc":"**The exact criterion.** The damped ratio drops below its undamped value\nexactly when the cross-weighted denominator energies dominate:\n`R τ ≤ R 0 ↔ ∑ᵢⱼ aᵢbⱼ e^{-Dⱼτ} ≤ ∑ᵢⱼ aᵢbⱼ e^{-Cᵢτ}`. Calculus-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.GibbsRatioMonotonicity.Z_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.GibbsRatioMonotonicity.Z_pos","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GibbsRatioMonotonicity.lean#L65-L71","doc":"A Gibbs sum with non-negative amplitudes, at least one positive, is\npositive — the standing non-degeneracy hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.GibbsRatioMonotonicity.Z_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.GibbsRatioMonotonicity.Z_zero","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GibbsRatioMonotonicity.lean#L61-L63","doc":"At `τ = 0` the damping is trivial and `Z` is the plain amplitude sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.GibbsRatioMonotonicity.Z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.GibbsRatioMonotonicity.Z","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GibbsRatioMonotonicity.lean#L57-L59","doc":"The damped (Gibbs / partition-function) sum `Z(τ) = ∑ aᵢ e^{-Cᵢ τ}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}